  "edition": "Philosophia theologiae ancillans (Oxford: T. Robinson & R. Davis, 1658; Editi priori correctior). Wing B887. IA bim_early-english-books-1641-1700_philosophia-theologi-an_baron-robert_1658. Exercitatio Prima Art. I-XII De Ente & Essentia (FULL first exercise densify complete for declared Prima scope; not whole Philosophia, 213 pp). First edition Andreapoli 1621 (Rabanus). Later Exercitationes remain.",
  "section_count": 12,
  "blurb": "Robert Baron — First Exercise On Being and Essence from the 1658 Oxford Latin of Philosophia theologiae ancillans. Covers Art. I-XII (necessary being through whether the personal subsistence of the Logos is communicated to humanity / ubiquity by that subsistence). Exercitatio Prima densify complete for this work's declared Prima scope; the rest of the Philosophia (213 pp / later Exercitationes) remains.",
  "era_note": "Baron wrote in the early seventeenth century as Reformed philosophy professor at St Salvator's College, St Andrews. This is not a patristic work. It is a public-domain Latin Reformed retrieval on the same Fathers-site pipeline. The 1658 Oxford Latin is public domain. Do not treat the site as ante-Nicene only.",
